Z||000004||Cooter||08-22-2000||10:25 PM||||When my dad bought his new Silverado, he went through 10 (yes, 10!) rear differentials in less than 60,000 miles. One was replace at 58,000 miles and it went out at 61,000! Since it only had a 60K warrantee, the dealership said "Sorry, not our problem anymore." He kept the letter from some big-wig at GM that said that General Motors would not make any more repairs, and the copy of the check that a nice attorney got for him the same day.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
