Z||000011||Monkeyman||08-24-2000||07:04 AM||||Doc--It <B>is</B> interesting how things that are supposedly "American made" aren't and vice versa.  Take the "American made", true American motorcycle, the Harley Davidson.  Most of the parts are made elsewhere and most if it isn't even assembled in the US.  Technically, the Honda Goldwing is more "American made" than H/D.  Not only is it produced in America, but most of the parts are made here, too.  Before anyone says that it's owned by the Japanese  (therefore not American made), the motorcycle line/branch of Honda is wholly American owned and operated.||||reg||1
