Z||000014||frontal lobe||08-24-2000||04:34 PM||||Hi Monkeyman.  Yeah, made in the good old U.S. of A. ...sort of.  Whatever happened to that push a few years ago where they were putting the domestic content of cars on the window stickers.  Anyone remember that?  I don't buy new cars so maybe they still do it and I'm just unaware.<P>I only live about 3 miles from the main Harley-Davidson place.  I pass it every day on the way to work.  I have several somewhat higher up employees as patients:  vp of licensing (trademark cop for counterfeit stuff like logos, shirts, etc.), head project engineer of chassis development, head of Harley's race team (lots of healed fractures there and a few false teeth), and the president's daughter.  Seems like a good company to work for so at least some jobs here in the U.S., but lots of foreign manufactured parts, for sure.<P>It was fun talking to them when they were going to fuel-injection for the engines instead of carburetors.  The engineers were going crazy trying to program the engines to misfire at idle about 2.5% of the time to try to artificially reproduce the "lumpy" idle of the carbed version to give it that characteristic Harley sound.  Interesting, but I don't know what it has to do with the impala.  Sorry, everyone, I'm getting off course.||||reg||1
